                <pb facs="0772" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg760"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">752.822/3: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-21T18:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Your 47, August 18, 9 p.m. We earnestly hope that the Liberian Government
                    will take no action on the Spanish proposals pending our further study of the
                    matter, the results of which will be communicated to you shortly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
